.TH UPTIME 1
.SH NAME
uptime - display guest uptime, process count and load averages
.SH SYNOPSIS
uptime
.SH DESCRIPTION
Displays elapsed guest time, occupied and total process slots, and the kernel's
one, five and fifteen minute load averages. Process slots include this utility
and unreaped zombies. There is no login-session accounting.
.PP
Time follows the host monotonic clock. Host pauses count toward uptime;
checkpoint downtime does not. Calendar corrections cannot change uptime.
The underlying 32-bit decisecond counter
wraps after approximately 13.6 years of guest uptime.
.SH OPTIONS
--help displays usage.
.SH SEE ALSO
free(1), ps(1), time(1)
